        "original_id": "bf0d11d5-4823-56ef-b795-97321972f368",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: A Woman Called Moses\n- People: Harriet Tubman\n- Concepts: Underground Railroad, American Civil War, abolitionism, humanitarianism\n\nFacts:\n- Harriet Tubman, born Araminta Ross, lived from about 1822 to March 10, 1913.\n- Harriet Tubman was an American abolitionist, humanitarian, and an armed scout and spy for the United States Army during the American Civil War.\n- Harriet Tubman escaped slavery and helped organize the Underground Railroad.\n- Harriet Tubman led dozens of African Americans from enslavement in the Southern United States to freedom in the Northern states and Canada.\n- A Woman Called Moses is a television miniseries based on the life of Harriet Tubman.",
